+# Privacy implementation and third-party audit
+
+Scope: the static Daily Grind site in this repository. Audit date: 2026-11-08.
+
+## Data inventory and minimization
+
+The site collects no form data and runs no client JavaScript. There are no analytics, cookies, local/session storage, visitor IDs, fingerprinting, pixels, remote fonts, embedded widgets, or reporting endpoints. No consent banner is needed for the current implementation because it sets no optional tracking technologies. Keep the website usable without consent or an account.
+
+The hosting provider necessarily receives IP addresses, request paths, and HTTP headers. Its identity, log retention, subprocessors, and deletion controls cannot be determined from this repository. Before production, record those facts and update the public privacy notice with actual hosting practices. Disable optional analytics and request-body logging, omit query strings and authentication material from logs, restrict log access, and use the shortest justified retention period. Never include personal information, access tokens, or payment details in URLs, static HTML, bundled files, or logs.
+
+## Third-party audit
+
+| Component | Finding | Handling |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash hero photo | Previously requested directly by every visitor, exposing network/request metadata to images.unsplash.com. | Existing stock photo downloaded to assets/coffee.jpg at development time. Visitors now fetch it from this site's origin. Source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085 . No runtime Unsplash request. |
+| Fonts and CSS | System fonts; no font provider. | Styles served locally; no external stylesheet or import. |
+| Client scripts, trackers, SDKs | None present. | CSP disables all scripts and network API connections; audit fails when a client script is added. |
+| Production packages | No runtime dependencies. | Static build uses Node built-ins only. |
+| Development start command | Existing pnpm dlx statikk command resolves an external package. | Development tooling only; excluded from the build artifact. It is not the production security-header configuration. |
+| Hosting | Not configured in this repository. | Confirm provider processing, logging, retention, HTTPS, and header support before deployment. |
+
+Re-run `npm test` for every change. Before adding a vendor, document purpose, transmitted fields, retention, deletion, subprocessors, and consent requirements. Prefer a local asset or no collection. Any new client code, endpoints, external resources, or production dependencies require updating this audit and its checks deliberately. These static checks guard this small site's current architecture; they are not a general HTML sanitizer or a completed audit of the hosting provider.
+
+## Security headers and deployment
+
+Run `npm run build` and deploy only `dist/` to a static HTTPS host. The build allowlist excludes source tooling and internal documentation. `_headers` supplies headers for hosts supporting that format, such as Netlify or Cloudflare Pages static assets. Other hosts must translate these rules into their own response configuration. Arbitrary static servers, including the existing development start command, may ignore `_headers`.
+
+The policy allows only local images and styles. Scripts, connections, forms, frames, workers, objects, and remote fonts are blocked. HTML contains a matching CSP fallback and no-referrer metadata; frame-ancestors, HSTS, Permissions-Policy, and other response-only protections require the actual HTTP headers. HSTS applies after an HTTPS response; configure HTTPS and an HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect at the host. Subdomain HSTS is intentionally not asserted without knowing subdomain ownership. No CSP reports are collected because reports can expose URLs and visitor information.
+
+Responses disable caching, browser permissions, cross-origin resource reuse, opener access, MIME sniffing, DNS prefetching, and framing. On deployment, verify these headers on both HTML pages, assets, and error responses using the hosting configuration or an HTTP header inspection tool. No deployed host or browser verification was performed as part of this implementation.
+
+## Future accounts and transactions
+
+The original public GET logout link was removed: this site has no session implementation. Existing account, rewards, menu, and ordering links do not implement those services. Do not collect credentials, payment information, or personal details until a backend and its privacy notice exist. A real logout must use a server-validated POST with CSRF protection. Any future session should use Secure, HttpOnly, appropriately scoped SameSite cookies, short lifetimes, rotation, and server-side invalidation. Validate data on the server, enforce authorization, minimize required fields, define deletion/retention, encrypt transport and stored sensitive data, and keep secrets out of client code. Review the restrictive form/connect CSP deliberately when introducing those features.
